{"id": "tea:aruni-upanisad:1", "source": "src:aruni-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Āruṇi goes to Prajāpati's world and asks how he can abandon all works; Prajāpati: give up sons, brothers, relatives, topknot, sacred thread, sacrifice, Vedic study and the worlds above and below; take staff, loincloth and cloth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa", "cpt:renunciant-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:uddalaka-aruni", "tch:prajapati"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aruni-upanisad:2", "source": "src:aruni-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The renouncer places the fires in the stomach-fire and the Gāyatrī in his speech; he abandons the thread in water or on the ground; he may renounce from any stage.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aruni-upanisad:3", "source": "src:aruni-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "'I am Brahman'; the thread is Brahman as that which 'points out' (sūcana); saying three times 'I have renounced', he grants 'fearlessness to all beings from me'; he takes a bamboo staff with the mantra 'friend, protect me'; he eats as medicine and guards celibacy, non-injury, non-possession and truth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite", "cpt:inner-sikha-yajnopavita"], "practices": ["prc:sannyasa-diksa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aruni-upanisad:4", "source": "src:aruni-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "He uses a bowl of earth, gourd or wood; he stays in one place in the rains and wanders the other eight months alone or with one companion.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "practices": ["prc:parivrajya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aruni-upanisad:5", "source": "src:aruni-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5"}, "paraphrase": "Knowing this, he abandons the palāśa, bilva or udumbara staff, deerskin, girdle and thread (of studentship); this is the highest place of Viṣṇu which the sages ever see (quoting the Ṛgveda).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
